A||||5||dmclaugh10||Vapor Cannister
Z||000000||dmclaugh10||08-14-99||04:42 PM||||I just purchased an 84 2M4 and was doing my first initial "poking around" in the engine compartment.  I noticed that the vapor cannister under the DS louver has only one 5/32" hose attached.  The hose fitting marked vac is just sitting there.  I assume this can't be right??  Is there supposed to ba another hose??  If so, to where??  I can't find a darn thing in the Haynes book. <p>BTW, the one hose that is attached is badly cracked, so I've gotta dink with it anyway...
Z||000001||theogre||08-14-99||05:45 PM||||routing for that device is on the VECI lable.<p>one hose, the big one, goes to manifild vac.<br>the other goes to a port on the TBI
Z||000002||dmclaugh10||08-14-99||06:31 PM||||Thanks, that helped...  I found the vapor cannister and it is connected correctly.  Unfortunately, I am even more confused.  This was not the cannister directly under the louver that I was referring to.  This looks like a large tin can with two fittings on the end.  Any idea what that is??  Sounds like it is a stupid question, but I'm stumped.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-14-99||06:53 PM||||Is it for the cruise control?
Z||000004||theogre||08-14-99||07:36 PM||||does it look like a juice can? could be a vacuum reserve. If it is, one side goes to manifold vac, the other to the where-ever it goes. It has a check valve on top so that when manifold vac drops, the can stays at high vacuum to run whatever it's connected to.<p>If it's on the wall of the trunk, and has a linkage to the throttle. your messing with the cruise unit.
Z||000005||dmclaugh10||08-14-99||08:00 PM||||Bingo...<p>It is the cruise (and yes, it does look like a juice can)  Perhaps that explains why the cruise doesn't work.  <p>Thanks for all the help.  Now I have a clue how to dig in.
